  "before_edn": "{:db/id 17592186059672 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186059500 :question/id #uuid \"35535b08-b3d8-5037-a821-6815577169d2\" :question/math-academy-id \"e-3618\" :question/problem \"Without using a calculator, find the exact value of $$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\sin{\\\\left(\\\\dfrac{\\\\pi}{24}\\\\right)}\\\\cos{\\\\left(\\\\dfrac{\\\\pi}{24}\\\\right)}\\\\cos{\\\\left(\\\\dfrac{\\\\pi}{12}\\\\right)}.\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\sin{x}\\\\cos{x} = \\\\sin{2x}\\n$$\\n\\nSubstituting $x=\\\\dfrac{\\\\pi}{24}$ into the above, we get\\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\sin\\\\left(\\\\dfrac{\\\\pi}{24}\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(\\\\dfrac{\\\\pi}{24}\\\\right) = \\\\sin\\\\left(2\\\\cdot \\\\dfrac{\\\\pi}{24}\\\\right)\\n$$\\n\\nwhich simplifies as\\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\sin\\\\left(\\\\dfrac{\\\\pi}{24}\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(\\\\dfrac{\\\\pi}{24}\\\\right) = \\\\sin\\\\left(\\\\dfrac{\\\\pi}{12}\\\\right) .\\n$$\\n\\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{24}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{24}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right) & =\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\left[2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{24}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{24}\\\\right)\\\\right]\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right) \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\\\dfrac{\\\\pi}{12},$ we can further simplify the above expression: \\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right) & =\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\left[2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)\\\\right] \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\left[\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(2\\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)\\\\right] \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{6}\\\\right) \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{2} \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{8}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore,\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\sin{\\\\left(\\\\dfrac{\\\\pi}{24}\\\\right)}\\\\cos{\\\\left(\\\\dfrac{\\\\pi}{24}\\\\right)}\\\\cos{\\\\left(\\\\dfrac{\\\\pi}{12}\\\\right)} = \\\\dfrac{1}{8}.\\n$$\"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid \"d820aa9f-7c02-53b5-9b09-c25ee59dbdaf\" :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id 17592186696444 :question-generator/id #uuid \"fdcddb08-a624-5329-9ae7-ffbc6389059f\" :question-generator/script \"generators/42/42828256eebf01d54122ec536d7edac92cec16cec2e2663fc8c82ce9b8d226ea/generator.py\"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186060239 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"5f5e037a-d907-5e75-8572-a21f2f100b86\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{2}\" :db/id 17592186288697} {:answer/id #uuid \"6b4c0f05-ccdb-59d1-bb07-0330ee61384f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{2}}{2}\" :db/id 17592186288788} {:answer/id #uuid \"add73e65-c6fc-54b3-86a9-efe0ea9d1061\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1+\\\\sqrt{3}}{2}\" :db/id 17592186289183} {:answer/id #uuid \"bfeaf92c-dcea-5028-acba-166e92cd2d93\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{2}\" :db/id 17592186289300} {:answer/id #uuid \"fc31e4ba-f99c-51b0-b6f7-de76a067ff38\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{2}\" :db/id 17592186289697}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"5f5e037a-d907-5e75-8572-a21f2f100b86\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{2}\" :db/id 17592186288697} :answer-field/id #uuid \"b85596f7-12df-574c-9e94-581ddb2bf096\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186290132}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"b22f045c-0b9c-53f1-b536-66fda02ca447\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-24361\" :question/problem \"Find the exact value of $4\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘}).$\" :question/worked-solution \"First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\n$$\\n\\nSubstituting $x={7.5}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘}) & =\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\\\cdot {7.5}^{∘})\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nwhich simplifies as\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘}) & =\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡({15}^{∘}).\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}4\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘}) & =2\\\\cdot 2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘}) \\\\\\\\  & =2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡({15}^{∘})\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘})\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x={15}^{∘},$ we can further simplify the above expression: \\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡{15}^{∘}\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡{15}^{∘}=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\\\cdot {15}^{∘})=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡({30}^{∘})\\n$$\\n\\nTherefore,\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}4\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘}) & =\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡({30}^{∘})=\\\\frac{1}{2}.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186060243 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"93710ca5-6027-591d-969f-097bebd99547\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{2}\\\\sin \\\\left(\\\\frac{π}{3}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186058101} {:answer/id #uuid \"dafb79ee-0595-52df-b01e-9c1753d35db9\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\sin \\\\left(\\\\frac{π}{6}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186058102} {:answer/id #uuid \"e1131cf8-b01f-5702-9ca2-a730156984f7\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{2}\\\\sin \\\\left(\\\\frac{π}{6}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186058103} {:answer/id #uuid \"3af60303-8273-5e10-9f8e-89a0cc111a4a\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"3\\\\sin \\\\left(\\\\frac{π}{6}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186058104} {:answer/id #uuid \"7b156a1e-b747-5820-8472-2b68ebe1b1db\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\sin \\\\left(\\\\frac{π}{3}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186058105}] :answer-field/id #uuid \"df1354db-d1d7-54db-baba-68ca0802536b\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186058100}] :question/id #uuid \"0ab58d1b-4097-516b-91bf-48c130e66ed2\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-24648\" :question/problem \"What is $$\\n\\\\displaystyle 6\\\\sin \\\\left(\\\\frac{π}{12}\\\\right)\\\\cos \\\\left(\\\\frac{π}{12}\\\\right)\\\\cos \\\\left(\\\\frac{π}{6}\\\\right)\\n$$?\"} {:db/id 17592186233282 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"18c9b4b1-1095-5f9b-afce-633347485f56\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{5}{2}\\\\operatorname{csc}⁡({75}^{∘})\" :db/id 17592186250770} {:answer/id #uuid \"299c5f87-5d49-5061-92a3-1c662ad07f92\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{5}{2}\" :db/id 17592186250909} {:answer/id #uuid \"70aa70e8-91d7-536f-ae22-f835158dcb12\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"5\\\\operatorname{csc}⁡({75}^{∘})\" :db/id 17592186251473} {:answer/id #uuid \"aeec17ba-9e38-5bb4-bd85-072a01d4cd00\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"5\" :db/id 17592186252077} {:answer/id #uuid \"eeb91b61-0767-56e9-b516-9be479319ff9\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"5\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡({150}^{∘})\" :db/id 17592186252645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"aeec17ba-9e38-5bb4-bd85-072a01d4cd00\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"5\" :db/id 17592186252077} :answer-field/id #uuid \"6946fb4a-fa21-51f2-b279-830394eb4469\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186252998}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"8883bfa3-8f36-5e8a-8a63-990442c2b246\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-120087\" :question/problem \"$10\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡({75}^{∘})\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡({75}^{∘})\\\\operatorname{csc}⁡({150}^{∘})=$\" :question/worked-solution \"First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\n$$\\n\\nSubstituting $x={75}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡({75}^{∘})\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡({75}^{∘}) & =\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\\\cdot {75}^{∘})=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡({150}^{∘})\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}10\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡({75}^{∘})\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡({75}^{∘})\\\\operatorname{csc}⁡({150}^{∘}) & =5\\\\cdot [2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡({75}^{∘})\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡({75}^{∘})]\\\\operatorname{csc}⁡({150}^{∘}) \\\\\\\\  & =5\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡({150}^{∘})\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡({150}^{∘})} \\\\\\\\  & =5.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186233283 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"19bb82ee-2583-57ae-92ec-48971505d385\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-120094\" :question/problem \"Find the exact value of $$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{sec}\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)}{\\\\operatorname{sin}\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)}.\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}x\\\\operatorname{cos}x=\\\\operatorname{sin}2x\\n$$\\n\\nSubstituting $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}$ into the above, we get\\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)=\\\\operatorname{sin}\\\\left(2\\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)\\n$$\\n\\nwhich simplifies as\\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)=\\\\operatorname{sin}\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right).\\n$$\\n\\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{sec}\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)}{\\\\operatorname{sin}\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)} & =\\\\frac{2\\\\operatorname{sec}\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)}{2\\\\operatorname{sin}\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)} \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{2\\\\operatorname{sec}\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)}{\\\\operatorname{sin}\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)} \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{2}{\\\\operatorname{sin}\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}$, we can further simplify the above expression: \\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{2}{\\\\operatorname{sin}\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)} & =\\\\frac{4}{2\\\\operatorname{sin}\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)} \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{4}{\\\\operatorname{sin}\\\\left(2\\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)} \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{4}{\\\\operatorname{sin}\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{4}\\\\right)} \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{4}{\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\\\right)} \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{8}{\\\\sqrt{2}} \\\\\\\\  & =4\\\\sqrt{2}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186253642 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"3c52498f-1f9e-501c-8891-4f23833a7182\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{csc}⁡({70}^{∘})\" :db/id 17592186251055} {:answer/id #uuid \"42ccec5d-e7d6-5db9-9f02-95edda5815f8\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"1\" :db/id 17592186251110} {:answer/id #uuid \"8bbb0dd1-6513-52a9-ad30-0f8d0db15d68\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\" :db/id 17592186251732} {:answer/id #uuid \"a80d5949-2bf5-5546-8841-d404bb011aa1\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡({140}^{∘})\" :db/id 17592186252003} {:answer/id #uuid \"e2aab337-ae1d-502e-b101-5ee4d4cf30ca\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\operatorname{csc}⁡({70}^{∘})\" :db/id 17592186252546}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"8bbb0dd1-6513-52a9-ad30-0f8d0db15d68\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\" :db/id 17592186251732} :answer-field/id #uuid \"3aec94b6-0548-5717-9741-10366c1cf83c\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186252904}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"8280d3f1-0c7e-5f24-8bb1-95c62d7445a7\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-120088\" :question/problem \"$4\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡({70}^{∘})\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡({70}^{∘})\\\\operatorname{csc}⁡({140}^{∘})=$\" :question/worked-solution \"First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\n$$\\n\\nSubstituting $x={70}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡({70}^{∘})\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡({70}^{∘}) & =\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\\\cdot {70}^{∘})=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡({140}^{∘})\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}4\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡({70}^{∘})\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡({70}^{∘})\\\\operatorname{csc}⁡({140}^{∘}) & =2\\\\cdot [2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡({70}^{∘})\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡({70}^{∘})]\\\\operatorname{csc}⁡({140}^{∘}) \\\\\\\\  & =2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡({140}^{∘})\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡({140}^{∘})} \\\\\\\\  & =2.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186253643 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"04698c75-dc83-5fbb-8f53-9052909b1e30\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186250585} {:answer/id #uuid \"1b2c3035-0235-5603-a72a-eb385d8843e0\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186250786} {:answer/id #uuid \"6012bda1-9035-5aff-82de-2b534c046c57\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186251340} {:answer/id #uuid \"9aad87db-038e-549a-b557-3d3499e0f30c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186251882} {:answer/id #uuid \"df46eab3-2fa6-5ef3-9539-002572011a52\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186252521}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"6012bda1-9035-5aff-82de-2b534c046c57\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186251340} :answer-field/id #uuid \"e90d146b-981f-56ed-88e6-d9ffffc3ab01\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186253212}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"91b3ae38-a411-55e5-ba0c-b0976c1d82dd\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-120093\" :question/problem \"$$\\n\\\\displaystyle 8\\\\,\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{32}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{32}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)=\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\n$$\\n\\nSubstituting $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{32}$ into the above, we get\\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{32}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{32}\\\\right)=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(2\\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\pi }{32}\\\\right)\\n$$\\n\\nwhich simplifies as\\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{32}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{32}\\\\right)=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right).\\n$$\\n\\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}8\\\\,\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{32}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{32}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right) & =4\\\\left[2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{32}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{32}\\\\right)\\\\right]\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right) \\\\\\\\  & =4\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16},$ we can further simplify the above expression: \\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}4\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right) & =2\\\\left[2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)\\\\right] \\\\\\\\  & =2\\\\left[\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(2\\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)\\\\right] \\\\\\\\  & =2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right).\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186290559 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"250cdf52-80dd-5fc2-af4b-70ef347a1cea\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{4}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186288273} {:answer/id #uuid \"3fd9b186-aadf-56c5-aa56-1a4655188af6\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{2}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186288467} {:answer/id #uuid \"aa4e972a-a6ae-5ee9-939d-472e588fddcd\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{2}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186289160} {:answer/id #uuid \"dd44e3ed-170a-5c64-abc8-da906810e3b4\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{4}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186289505} {:answer/id #uuid \"e97836dd-63c8-53a9-9a9c-9ddec55ceab1\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{2}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186289583}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"3fd9b186-aadf-56c5-aa56-1a4655188af6\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{2}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186288467} :answer-field/id #uuid \"dd8d3d20-451b-5d5a-b8e5-ba16d376b2a2\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186290201}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"4270d786-b50e-5319-88f8-bca386712273\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-24645\" :question/problem \"$$\\n\\\\displaystyle 4\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{4}\\\\right)=\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\n$$\\n\\nSubstituting $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(2\\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)\\n$$\\n\\nwhich simplifies as\\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{4}\\\\right).\\n$$\\n\\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}4\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{4}\\\\right) & =2\\\\left[2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)\\\\right]\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{4}\\\\right) \\\\\\\\  & =2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{4}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{4}\\\\right)\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nNow, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{4}$, we can further simplify the above expression: \\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}4\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{4}\\\\right) & =2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{4}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{4}\\\\right) \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(2\\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\pi }{4}\\\\right) \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{2}\\\\right)\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186290562 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"21623035-5d3b-54b0-b966-85086e882ee3\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\" :db/id 17592186288244} {:answer/id #uuid \"327ce358-2120-579c-a825-a49f79276978\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4\\\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{5}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186288362} {:answer/id #uuid \"462fdeb4-069c-543e-84f4-6256b0c7292e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{2\\\\pi }{5}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186288512} {:answer/id #uuid \"4691cd9d-d70d-5609-bda6-07f12d1b3808\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4\" :db/id 17592186288515} {:answer/id #uuid \"6381d420-eb79-5f12-aa11-1fa09a350b57\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{4\\\\pi }{5}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186288728}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"4691cd9d-d70d-5609-bda6-07f12d1b3808\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4\" :db/id 17592186288515} :answer-field/id #uuid \"b3e9dae2-f4ee-56c2-b632-6441b7a7809a\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186290123}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"f30309d1-f3e3-55ac-be8a-acbe0c0f980a\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-24650\" :question/problem \"$$\\n\\\\displaystyle 8\\\\,\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{5}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{5}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{2\\\\pi }{5}\\\\right)=\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\n$$\\n\\nSubstituting $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{5}$ into the above, we get\\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{5}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{5}\\\\right)=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(2\\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\pi }{5}\\\\right)=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{2\\\\pi }{5}\\\\right).\\n$$\\n\\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}8\\\\,\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{5}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{5}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{2\\\\pi }{5}\\\\right) & =4\\\\cdot \\\\left[2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{5}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{5}\\\\right)\\\\right]\\\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{2\\\\pi }{5}\\\\right) \\\\\\\\  & =4\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{2\\\\pi }{5}\\\\right)\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{2\\\\pi }{5}\\\\right)} \\\\\\\\  & =4\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186290577 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"39c3ecbd-17ed-5b06-b654-653c3049502e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{2}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186288427} {:answer/id #uuid \"4c1c7922-d73e-55f5-a376-2d36947a8151\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{4}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186288559} {:answer/id #uuid \"5af6a861-2ad4-55c6-9de1-23e3e121be7c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{2}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186288666} {:answer/id #uuid \"640a6f06-222f-5050-8d99-73191247207c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{2}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186288735} {:answer/id #uuid \"6c6c9ed9-62d6-592d-8648-4a352af8d6c9\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{4}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186288797}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"640a6f06-222f-5050-8d99-73191247207c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{2}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186288735} :answer-field/id #uuid \"ef225602-1693-5ca7-8c43-67f2e54eda30\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186290226}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"87e7afa8-1798-5127-a9ff-a08924db07de\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-24792\" :question/problem \"Find the exact value of $$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)}{\\\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{4}\\\\right)}.\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\n$$\\n\\nSubstituting $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(2\\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)\\n$$\\n\\nwhich simplifies as\\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{4}\\\\right).\\n$$\\n\\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)}{\\\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{4}\\\\right)} & =\\\\frac{\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\cdot 2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)}{\\\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{4}\\\\right)} \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{4}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{4}\\\\right)\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{4}$, we can further simplify the above expression: \\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)}{\\\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{4}\\\\right)} & =\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{4}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{4}\\\\right) \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\cdot 2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{4}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{4}\\\\right) \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(2\\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\pi }{4}\\\\right) \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{2}\\\\right)\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186302344 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"b64c24fe-86c0-528a-a80a-d441c9376663\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{8}\" :db/id 17592186300870}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"b64c24fe-86c0-528a-a80a-d441c9376663\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{8}\" :db/id 17592186300870} :answer-field/id #uuid \"51f40c8d-649b-5cc5-8611-1a3900cfece1\" :answer-field/key \"field-1\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186301496}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"6a88295e-a9f4-5381-9209-7cdc6c3b161d\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-327716\" :question/problem \"Find the exact value of $$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{24}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{24}\\\\right)}{\\\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)}.\\n$$\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{24}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{24}\\\\right)}{\\\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)}=\\n$$\\n{{field-1}}\" :question/worked-solution \"First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\n$$\\n\\nSubstituting $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{24}$ into the above, we get\\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{24}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{24}\\\\right)=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(2\\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\pi }{24}\\\\right)\\n$$\\n\\nwhich simplifies as\\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{24}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{24}\\\\right)=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)\\n$$\\n\\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{24}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{24}\\\\right)}{\\\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)} & =\\\\frac{\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)}{\\\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)} \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}$, we can further simplify the above expression: \\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{24}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{24}\\\\right)}{\\\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)} & =\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right) \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\cdot 2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right) \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\cdot \\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(2\\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right) \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{6}\\\\right) \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{2} \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{8}.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186302395 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"04c58237-1e79-538c-ba35-64864273d7c4\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-8\" :db/id 17592186299953}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"04c58237-1e79-538c-ba35-64864273d7c4\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-8\" :db/id 17592186299953} :answer-field/id #uuid \"f6c6a4ff-0ad2-5a80-99b9-227f85929a6d\" :answer-field/key \"field-1\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186302015}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"4fabc70d-25ca-5a30-9a52-90a915524efa\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-328087\" :question/problem \"Find the exact value of $$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)}{\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{24}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{24}\\\\right)}.\\n$$\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)}{\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{24}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{24}\\\\right)}=\\n$$\\n{{field-1}}\" :question/worked-solution \"First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\n$$\\n\\nSubstituting $x=\\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{24}$ into the above, we get\\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{24}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{24}\\\\right)=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(2\\\\cdot \\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{24}\\\\right)\\n$$\\n\\nwhich simplifies as\\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{24}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{24}\\\\right)=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right).\\n$$\\n\\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)}{\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{24}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{24}\\\\right)} & =\\\\frac{2\\\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)}{2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{24}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{24}\\\\right)} \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{2\\\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)}{\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)} \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{2}{\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{12}$, we can further simplify the above expression: \\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{2}{\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)} & =\\\\frac{2\\\\cdot 2}{2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)} \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{4}{\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(2\\\\cdot \\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)} \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{4}{\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{7\\\\pi }{6}\\\\right)} \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{4}{\\\\left(-\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\right)} \\\\\\\\  & =-8\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186323805 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"d6dcfdc0-0425-58da-9863-8d71fb334ef1\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{2}}{8}\" :db/id 17592186322824}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"d6dcfdc0-0425-58da-9863-8d71fb334ef1\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{2}}{8}\" :db/id 17592186322824} :answer-field/id #uuid \"1ebc2e95-bd33-54eb-b38e-19227069b90a\" :answer-field/key \"field-1\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186323226}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"5749738c-9ac0-51f9-9b71-e3d7fdfbde49\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-364639\" :question/problem \"Find the exact value of $$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)}{\\\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)}.\\n$$\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)}{\\\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)}=\\n$$\\n{{field-1}}\" :question/worked-solution \"First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\n$$\\n\\nSubstituting $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}$ into the above, we get\\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(2\\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)\\n$$\\n\\nwhich simplifies as\\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)\\n$$\\n\\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)}{\\\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)} & =\\\\frac{\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)}{\\\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)} \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}$, we can further simplify the above expression: \\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{16}\\\\right)}{\\\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)} & =\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right) \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\cdot 2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right) \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\cdot \\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(2\\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\pi }{8}\\\\right) \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{4}\\\\right) \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{2}}{8}.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186323806 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"5527a2df-a2d6-5eff-8e35-66b2ae6e3318\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{8}\" :db/id 17592186321819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"5527a2df-a2d6-5eff-8e35-66b2ae6e3318\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{8}\" :db/id 17592186321819} :answer-field/id #uuid \"bdcaa383-804e-5471-975f-ae53c9f7d704\" :answer-field/key \"field-1\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186323540}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"e9ff4e40-981d-5344-8025-a467141eea82\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-364640\" :question/problem \"Find the exact value of $$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)}{\\\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{6}\\\\right)}.\\n$$\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)}{\\\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{6}\\\\right)}=\\n$$\\n{{field-1}}\" :question/worked-solution \"First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\n$$\\n\\nSubstituting $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}$ into the above, we get\\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(2\\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)\\n$$\\n\\nwhich simplifies as\\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{6}\\\\right)\\n$$\\n\\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)}{\\\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{6}\\\\right)} & =\\\\frac{\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{6}\\\\right)}{\\\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{6}\\\\right)} \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{6}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{6}\\\\right)\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{6}$, we can further simplify the above expression: \\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{12}\\\\right)}{\\\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{6}\\\\right)} & =\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{6}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{6}\\\\right) \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\cdot 2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{6}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{6}\\\\right) \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\cdot \\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(2\\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\pi }{6}\\\\right) \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{3}\\\\right) \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{8}.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186345243 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"6624c503-a440-59c9-8f2d-03632a1ac414\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{2}\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{2\\\\pi }{7}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186343105} {:answer/id #uuid \"9a938235-b3f4-54c2-b79f-6fe77fb80b1e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"3\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{2\\\\pi }{7}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186343599} {:answer/id #uuid \"9dd4d77b-6b5a-5089-99a1-e818c683648e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"3\" :db/id 17592186343625} {:answer/id #uuid \"bb100409-5df2-5a5a-8228-1775440e2d46\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"3\\\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{7}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186343883} {:answer/id #uuid \"d99f783f-0b69-5884-9e2f-48416231f2b9\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{2}\" :db/id 17592186344148}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"9dd4d77b-6b5a-5089-99a1-e818c683648e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"3\" :db/id 17592186343625} :answer-field/id #uuid \"1748e2fb-ce8f-5df0-8345-b0b4c3f06cc8\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186344530}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"3d7f3236-aee5-5d63-80b7-2ecd442664e7\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-76660\" :question/problem \"$$\\n\\\\displaystyle 6\\\\,\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{7}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{7}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{2\\\\pi }{7}\\\\right)=\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\n$$\\n\\nSubstituting $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{7}$ into the above, we get\\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{7}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{7}\\\\right)=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(2\\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\pi }{7}\\\\right)=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{2\\\\pi }{7}\\\\right).\\n$$\\n\\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}6\\\\,\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{7}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{7}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{2\\\\pi }{7}\\\\right) & =3\\\\cdot \\\\left[2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{7}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{7}\\\\right)\\\\right]\\\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{2\\\\pi }{7}\\\\right) \\\\\\\\  & =3\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{2\\\\pi }{7}\\\\right)\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{2\\\\pi }{7}\\\\right)} \\\\\\\\  & =3\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186345244 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"11a1cebb-a7ec-573e-834f-5765dcecf952\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"6\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{5}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186342394} {:answer/id #uuid \"254c3227-d0aa-5723-a923-035c9df92844\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{2}\" :db/id 17592186342551} {:answer/id #uuid \"6ab0592e-6a5f-5609-ad32-dc332fbcc425\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"6\\\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{10}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186343147} {:answer/id #uuid \"83b4ab2f-a0ac-5b73-956c-314a45cef514\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"3\" :db/id 17592186343363} {:answer/id #uuid \"afff12a2-3582-5334-9126-b7ef6ab71ae1\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"3\\\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{10}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186343784}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"83b4ab2f-a0ac-5b73-956c-314a45cef514\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"3\" :db/id 17592186343363} :answer-field/id #uuid \"24cdb73d-8bf4-5a1b-9d30-d95b06bf3c8c\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186344560}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"c41ea86a-3b09-5773-9843-df888de284a4\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-76664\" :question/problem \"$$\\n\\\\displaystyle 6\\\\,\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{10}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{10}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{5}\\\\right)=\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\n$$\\n\\nSubstituting $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{10}$ into the above, we get\\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{10}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{10}\\\\right)=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(2\\\\cdot \\\\frac{\\\\pi }{10}\\\\right)=\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{5}\\\\right).\\n$$\\n\\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}6\\\\,\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{10}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{10}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{5}\\\\right) & =3\\\\cdot \\\\left[2\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{10}\\\\right)\\\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{10}\\\\right)\\\\right]\\\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{5}\\\\right) \\\\\\\\  & =3\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{5}\\\\right)\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{\\\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi }{5}\\\\right)} \\\\\\\\  & =3\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186696008 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"22155814-2e37-5e33-bac0-7171c896a0fc\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3\\\\sqrt{2}}{8}\" :db/id 17592186696010} {:answer/id #uuid \"65ada7bc-a1f0-53d7-a69a-e1c830bd9241\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3\\\\sqrt{3}}{8}\" :db/id 17592186696017} {:answer/id #uuid \"895d39bd-2973-5a32-8b58-8f1949d41b25\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{8}\" :db/id 17592186696018} {:answer/id #uuid \"ab20ebb6-bd86-5778-b38a-5eae9a602bbb\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3\\\\sqrt{3}}{16}\" :db/id 17592186696020} {:answer/id #uuid \"ff049149-7eb5-5670-9d67-5561e3e11044\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3\\\\sqrt{3}}{4}\" :db/id 17592186696024}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"65ada7bc-a1f0-53d7-a69a-e1c830bd9241\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3\\\\sqrt{3}}{8}\" :db/id 17592186696017} :answer-field/id #uuid \"b30b00d4-6a0d-5c61-a206-cd09af6d2cc1\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186696022}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"0abb88c3-b1d8-5fd6-9259-e93980f1b3ad\" :question/problem \"Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\\n$$\\n3\\\\sin(15^\\\\circ)\\\\cos(15^\\\\circ)\\\\cos(30^\\\\circ).\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"Use the double-angle identity in the form $\\\\sin x\\\\cos x=\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\sin(2x)$:\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\n3\\\\sin(15^\\\\circ)\\\\cos(15^\\\\circ)\\\\cos(30^\\\\circ)\\n&=\\\\frac{3}{2}\\\\sin(30^\\\\circ)\\\\cos(30^\\\\circ)\\\\\\\\\\n&=\\\\frac{3}{4}\\\\sin(60^\\\\circ)\\\\\\\\\\n&=\\\\frac{3}{4}\\\\cdot\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\\\\\\\\\n&=\\\\frac{3\\\\sqrt{3}}{8}.\\n\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\nThe identity is used twice: the angles progress from $15^\\\\circ$ to $30^\\\\circ$ to $60^\\\\circ$. Each use introduces a factor of $\\\\frac{1}{2}$.\"} {:db/id 17592186696009 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"a9ff46e3-0ea0-5dc2-8d04-4c4708045688\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-4\\\\sqrt{2}\" :db/id 17592186696019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"a9ff46e3-0ea0-5dc2-8d04-4c4708045688\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-4\\\\sqrt{2}\" :db/id 17592186696019} :answer-field/id #uuid \"5d3273ef-447e-5d04-b3a7-02bef4538847\" :answer-field/key \"field-1\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186696014}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"1043af1e-be8e-50e8-a088-c079feee421f\" :question/problem \"Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\sec\\\\left(\\\\frac{5\\\\pi}{8}\\\\right)}{\\\\sin\\\\left(\\\\frac{5\\\\pi}{16}\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(\\\\frac{5\\\\pi}{16}\\\\right)}.\\n$$\\n{{field-1}}\" :question/worked-solution \"First use $\\\\sin x\\\\cos x=\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\sin(2x)$ in the denominator. Then write secant as the reciprocal of cosine:\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\n\\\\frac{\\\\sec\\\\left(\\\\frac{5\\\\pi}{8}\\\\right)}{\\\\sin\\\\left(\\\\frac{5\\\\pi}{16}\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(\\\\frac{5\\\\pi}{16}\\\\right)}\\n&=\\\\frac{2\\\\sec\\\\left(\\\\frac{5\\\\pi}{8}\\\\right)}{\\\\sin\\\\left(\\\\frac{5\\\\pi}{8}\\\\right)}\\\\\\\\\\n&=\\\\frac{2}{\\\\sin\\\\left(\\\\frac{5\\\\pi}{8}\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(\\\\frac{5\\\\pi}{8}\\\\right)}\\\\\\\\\\n&=\\\\frac{4}{\\\\sin\\\\left(\\\\frac{5\\\\pi}{4}\\\\right)}.\\n\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\nThe last step uses the double-angle identity a second time. Since $\\\\frac{5\\\\pi}{4}$ lies in quadrant III, $\\\\sin\\\\left(\\\\frac{5\\\\pi}{4}\\\\right)=-\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{2}}{2}$. Therefore,\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{4}{-\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{2}}{2}}=-\\\\frac{8}{\\\\sqrt{2}}=-4\\\\sqrt{2}.\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186696011 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"47f0cf48-d111-57cb-8e12-2cc71f950d2a\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{2}}{2}\" :db/id 17592186696012} {:answer/id #uuid \"5f8ed73c-85b7-5fc2-a19a-a001a5ca7b8b\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{2}\" :db/id 17592186696015} {:answer/id #uuid \"645fb0d0-ca3b-53ea-97d6-693dd7883dea\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\sin\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{8}\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186696016} {:answer/id #uuid \"b0380848-af16-51fe-af42-6915027a3178\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\sqrt{2}\" :db/id 17592186696021} {:answer/id #uuid \"d6d5b322-4d69-5dd0-9b4e-9e5b5c3fb769\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{2}}{4}\" :db/id 17592186696023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"47f0cf48-d111-57cb-8e12-2cc71f950d2a\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{2}}{2}\" :db/id 17592186696012} :answer-field/id #uuid \"52d288e6-6a69-5bea-bfbb-8a58cf5588c8\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186696013}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"23700599-02b8-5b30-905e-86d4d7a86aa5\" :question/problem \"Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\\n$$\\n4\\\\sin\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{16}\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{16}\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{8}\\\\right).\\n$$\\nUse $2\\\\sin x\\\\cos x=\\\\sin(2x)$, first with $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{16}$ and then with $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{8}$.\" :question/worked-solution \"Let $E$ denote the given expression. Group a factor of $2$ with the first sine–cosine pair:\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\nE&=2\\\\left[2\\\\sin\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{16}\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{16}\\\\right)\\\\right]\\\\cos\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{8}\\\\right)\\\\\\\\\\n&=2\\\\sin\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{8}\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{8}\\\\right).\\n\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\nThe new sine has the same angle as the remaining cosine, so apply the identity again:\\n$$\\n2\\\\sin\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{8}\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{8}\\\\right)\\n=\\\\sin\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{4}\\\\right)=\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186696414 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"13538aaa-ca65-5d06-85af-2913f76d3a3f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{4}\" :db/id 17592186696410} {:answer/id #uuid \"4bb793f3-bbc6-5877-82d5-3fc01ed94b41\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{2}}{4}\" :db/id 17592186696417} {:answer/id #uuid \"663d514e-6784-5e2a-9ad8-d8f21ea6c235\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{1}{2}\" :db/id 17592186696424} {:answer/id #uuid \"afecf3fe-e744-5e83-b5da-be31d16572d3\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-1\" :db/id 17592186696432} {:answer/id #uuid \"f233d6e8-42ef-5432-848c-eec50e0252b3\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{1}{4}\" :db/id 17592186696441}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"afecf3fe-e744-5e83-b5da-be31d16572d3\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-1\" :db/id 17592186696432} :answer-field/id #uuid \"d1a32f35-a829-593c-aa5f-de7575807153\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186696435}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"1fe16984-8dc7-561a-bb43-80bc768dbed2\" :question/problem \"Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\\n$$\\n4\\\\,\\\\sin\\\\left(67.5^\\\\circ\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(67.5^\\\\circ\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(135^\\\\circ\\\\right).\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"Let $E$ denote the given expression. Use $\\\\sin x\\\\cos x=\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\sin(2x)$ first at $x=67.5^\\\\circ$ and then at $x=135^\\\\circ$. Each application introduces a factor of $\\\\frac{1}{2}$.\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\nE&=2\\\\,\\\\sin\\\\left(135^\\\\circ\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(135^\\\\circ\\\\right)\\\\\\\\&=\\\\sin\\\\left(270^\\\\circ\\\\right)\\n\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\nThe terminal sine is $\\\\sin\\\\left(270^\\\\circ\\\\right)=-1$.\\nTherefore,\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\nE&=\\\\left(-1\\\\right)\\\\\\\\&=-1.\\n\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186696420 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"15ec7ef2-a593-586c-abe6-8357e5e5e3da\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{16}\" :db/id 17592186696411} {:answer/id #uuid \"9a4c4936-1148-5e91-bd56-647d9ae1f4b6\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{8}\" :db/id 17592186696429} {:answer/id #uuid \"adda62d6-2d7b-5ef1-9867-71d8187fc3d9\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{2}\" :db/id 17592186696431} {:answer/id #uuid \"d9d97b2c-109b-5e43-9aee-a7bfdf3a3df7\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{4}\" :db/id 17592186696436} {:answer/id #uuid \"e491a915-a5fc-5aa7-85fb-6c2848d371cc\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{4}\" :db/id 17592186696438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"e491a915-a5fc-5aa7-85fb-6c2848d371cc\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{4}\" :db/id 17592186696438} :answer-field/id #uuid \"33e4d7ac-4a91-5c7f-b9ae-f4cc6bd2f0c9\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186696415}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"4ea294b3-11ab-5619-84a6-dff30ff4752b\" :question/problem \"Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\\n$$\\n2\\\\,\\\\sin\\\\left(15^\\\\circ\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(15^\\\\circ\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(30^\\\\circ\\\\right).\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"Let $E$ denote the given expression. Use $\\\\sin x\\\\cos x=\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\sin(2x)$ first at $x=15^\\\\circ$ and then at $x=30^\\\\circ$. Each application introduces a factor of $\\\\frac{1}{2}$.\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\nE&=\\\\sin\\\\left(30^\\\\circ\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(30^\\\\circ\\\\right)\\\\\\\\&=\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\,\\\\sin\\\\left(60^\\\\circ\\\\right)\\n\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\nThe terminal sine is $\\\\sin\\\\left(60^\\\\circ\\\\right)=\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{2}$.\\nTherefore,\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\nE&=\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\,\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\\\right)\\\\\\\\&=\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{4}.\\n\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186696423 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"1674d517-3220-5613-a583-37d0b9c0c82b\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{2}}{2}\" :db/id 17592186696412} {:answer/id #uuid \"4bb825f9-d4dc-5f97-ae4b-413bf0325abd\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"1\" :db/id 17592186696418} {:answer/id #uuid \"4e2ec0b1-45c1-5cd6-85c0-6622194f78b1\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{2}\" :db/id 17592186696419} {:answer/id #uuid \"a53a774e-91de-553f-aa96-c774adc6cb72\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{4}\" :db/id 17592186696430} {:answer/id #uuid \"b9291df2-e04f-523a-8831-0dbae8e1ff3c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{2}\" :db/id 17592186696433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"b9291df2-e04f-523a-8831-0dbae8e1ff3c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{2}\" :db/id 17592186696433} :answer-field/id #uuid \"6c3b92ef-5405-56a4-a7e3-e9d0af6d8066\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186696425}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"5f5f9ddc-cee0-5b98-973b-5ba53e1662a7\" :question/problem \"Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\\n$$\\n4\\\\,\\\\sin\\\\left(37.5^\\\\circ\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(37.5^\\\\circ\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(75^\\\\circ\\\\right).\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"Let $E$ denote the given expression. Use $\\\\sin x\\\\cos x=\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\sin(2x)$ first at $x=37.5^\\\\circ$ and then at $x=75^\\\\circ$. Each application introduces a factor of $\\\\frac{1}{2}$.\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\nE&=2\\\\,\\\\sin\\\\left(75^\\\\circ\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(75^\\\\circ\\\\right)\\\\\\\\&=\\\\sin\\\\left(150^\\\\circ\\\\right)\\n\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\nThe terminal sine is $\\\\sin\\\\left(150^\\\\circ\\\\right)=\\\\frac{1}{2}$.\\nTherefore,\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\nE&=\\\\left(\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\right)\\\\\\\\&=\\\\frac{1}{2}.\\n\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186696428 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"03e8236f-5bc5-5928-8b0a-698f064f11f2\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{2}}{8}\" :db/id 17592186696409} {:answer/id #uuid \"358d5334-c6eb-5dc3-be06-55b45b312580\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{4}\" :db/id 17592186696416} {:answer/id #uuid \"56bd2798-a433-5a51-9272-4ba01c0daa0a\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{2}\" :db/id 17592186696421} {:answer/id #uuid \"6e7eaae4-8493-5821-b061-0f2d51ebadd2\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{8}\" :db/id 17592186696426} {:answer/id #uuid \"ed79320e-c979-51fa-96c2-e4f89f02d0b4\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{8}\" :db/id 17592186696440}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"358d5334-c6eb-5dc3-be06-55b45b312580\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{4}\" :db/id 17592186696416} :answer-field/id #uuid \"da66bc2b-03f3-5724-ba09-06fb4670f5ce\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186696437}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"7802a331-7a6f-5235-bf01-b523c13fbb32\" :question/problem \"Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\\n$$\\n\\\\sin\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{8}\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{8}\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{4}\\\\right).\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"Let $E$ denote the given expression. Use $\\\\sin x\\\\cos x=\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\sin(2x)$ first at $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{8}$ and then at $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{4}$. Each application introduces a factor of $\\\\frac{1}{2}$.\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\nE&=\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\,\\\\sin\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{4}\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{4}\\\\right)\\\\\\\\&=\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\,\\\\sin\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{2}\\\\right)\\n\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\nThe terminal sine is $\\\\sin\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{2}\\\\right)=1$.\\nTherefore,\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\nE&=\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\,\\\\left(1\\\\right)\\\\\\\\&=\\\\frac{1}{4}.\\n\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186696434 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"1b003a3e-46aa-5c27-a97e-76ae302e2c21\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- 3 \\\\sqrt{2}\" :db/id 17592186696413} {:answer/id #uuid \"5ee0769e-9049-53b1-adc6-94bc3a327321\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{3 \\\\sqrt{2}}{2}\" :db/id 17592186696422} {:answer/id #uuid \"746e9be1-aadc-5c9f-a2a8-34e0d1c73565\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{3 \\\\sqrt{2}}{4}\" :db/id 17592186696427} {:answer/id #uuid \"fc07c100-67b9-5809-8eb2-0f90418917a3\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{3}{4}\" :db/id 17592186696442} {:answer/id #uuid \"fe81fdc4-1746-5bad-a138-deef587fc86b\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{3 \\\\sqrt{3}}{4}\" :db/id 17592186696443}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"746e9be1-aadc-5c9f-a2a8-34e0d1c73565\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{3 \\\\sqrt{2}}{4}\" :db/id 17592186696427} :answer-field/id #uuid \"e874ece7-3e44-5c21-9e81-be8ae3bd2318\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186696439}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"d0cbdd9c-621b-5b92-a56d-67d0c84d980b\" :question/problem \"Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\\n$$\\n6\\\\,\\\\sin\\\\left(56.25^\\\\circ\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(56.25^\\\\circ\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(112.5^\\\\circ\\\\right).\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"Let $E$ denote the given expression. Use $\\\\sin x\\\\cos x=\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\sin(2x)$ first at $x=56.25^\\\\circ$ and then at $x=112.5^\\\\circ$. Each application introduces a factor of $\\\\frac{1}{2}$.\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\nE&=3\\\\,\\\\sin\\\\left(112.5^\\\\circ\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(112.5^\\\\circ\\\\right)\\\\\\\\&=\\\\frac{3}{2}\\\\,\\\\sin\\\\left(225^\\\\circ\\\\right)\\n\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\nThe terminal sine is $\\\\sin\\\\left(225^\\\\circ\\\\right)=- \\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{2}}{2}$.\\nTherefore,\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\nE&=\\\\frac{3}{2}\\\\,\\\\left(- \\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\\\right)\\\\\\\\&=- \\\\frac{3 \\\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\\n\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186696466 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"08174645-ce91-560d-a4ed-f5f95a93d6d7\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3 \\\\sqrt{2}}{4}\" :db/id 17592186696461} {:answer/id #uuid \"1770c482-feee-5e70-a599-c3bfd8cf061a\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{4}\" :db/id 17592186696462} {:answer/id #uuid \"99d59b99-02a8-5666-94a5-cb1e15221fb0\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{8}\" :db/id 17592186696469} {:answer/id #uuid \"bfab0630-27c0-5588-a34c-76536916037f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3 \\\\sqrt{2}}{16}\" :db/id 17592186696475} {:answer/id #uuid \"c79305b8-4f9c-518d-bafd-0c7616948ec2\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3 \\\\sqrt{2}}{8}\" :db/id 17592186696477}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"c79305b8-4f9c-518d-bafd-0c7616948ec2\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3 \\\\sqrt{2}}{8}\" :db/id 17592186696477} :answer-field/id #uuid \"ab2049b0-91fe-5186-9e5c-79f4d5d2c863\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186696473}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"46b13209-07e2-546e-9832-02b898afa818\" :question/problem \"Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\\n$$\\n3\\\\,\\\\sin\\\\left(33.75^\\\\circ\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(33.75^\\\\circ\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(67.5^\\\\circ\\\\right).\\n$$\\nUse $2\\\\sin x\\\\cos x=\\\\sin(2x)$, first with $x=33.75^\\\\circ$ and then with $x=67.5^\\\\circ$.\" :question/worked-solution \"Let $E$ denote the given expression. Use $\\\\sin x\\\\cos x=\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\sin(2x)$ first at $x=33.75^\\\\circ$ and then at $x=67.5^\\\\circ$. Each application introduces a factor of $\\\\frac{1}{2}$.\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\nE&=\\\\frac{3}{2}\\\\,\\\\sin\\\\left(67.5^\\\\circ\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(67.5^\\\\circ\\\\right)\\\\\\\\&=\\\\frac{3}{4}\\\\,\\\\sin\\\\left(135^\\\\circ\\\\right)\\n\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\nThe terminal sine is $\\\\sin\\\\left(135^\\\\circ\\\\right)=\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{2}}{2}$.\\nTherefore,\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\nE&=\\\\frac{3}{4}\\\\,\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\\\right)\\\\\\\\&=\\\\frac{3 \\\\sqrt{2}}{8}.\\n\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186696472 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"1782c803-3007-5f83-84b0-e850ec7a7391\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{2}\" :db/id 17592186696463} {:answer/id #uuid \"2cb5a4ff-71f2-5baf-980a-cb21442ac802\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"6\" :db/id 17592186696464} {:answer/id #uuid \"c3d79b4e-dfdf-5187-88ff-fdea22364d28\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3 \\\\sqrt{3}}{2}\" :db/id 17592186696476} {:answer/id #uuid \"e29e96db-58d1-5a83-9857-f8731f8b5d3b\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"3\" :db/id 17592186696482} {:answer/id #uuid \"fe904c95-8f5f-5667-808b-7aa73bb2b5e5\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3 \\\\sqrt{2}}{2}\" :db/id 17592186696486}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"1782c803-3007-5f83-84b0-e850ec7a7391\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{2}\" :db/id 17592186696463} :answer-field/id #uuid \"0523e506-9246-5607-a9c8-e5465ee69eb7\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186696460}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"a6d7004b-efb4-5d6a-bc77-0990b992565b\" :question/problem \"Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\\n$$\\n6\\\\,\\\\sin\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{8}\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{8}\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{4}\\\\right).\\n$$\\nUse $2\\\\sin x\\\\cos x=\\\\sin(2x)$, first with $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{8}$ and then with $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{4}$.\" :question/worked-solution \"Let $E$ denote the given expression. Use $\\\\sin x\\\\cos x=\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\sin(2x)$ first at $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{8}$ and then at $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{4}$. Each application introduces a factor of $\\\\frac{1}{2}$.\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\nE&=3\\\\,\\\\sin\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{4}\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{4}\\\\right)\\\\\\\\&=\\\\frac{3}{2}\\\\,\\\\sin\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{2}\\\\right)\\n\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\nThe terminal sine is $\\\\sin\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{2}\\\\right)=1$.\\nTherefore,\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\nE&=\\\\frac{3}{2}\\\\,\\\\left(1\\\\right)\\\\\\\\&=\\\\frac{3}{2}.\\n\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186696479 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"40a91b96-341a-5cd8-8045-114b614109d9\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{32}\" :db/id 17592186696465} {:answer/id #uuid \"66ec7b86-0f5f-5a6c-9f8c-cbdc28df5c12\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{2}}{16}\" :db/id 17592186696467} {:answer/id #uuid \"a2e73bc8-691f-5620-b52d-5b2eacb05674\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{8}\" :db/id 17592186696471} {:answer/id #uuid \"b5376efb-175e-5c1e-9407-a885e73fe358\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{16}\" :db/id 17592186696474} {:answer/id #uuid \"d0649c4c-db0c-5e5d-8539-20d09f084937\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{16}\" :db/id 17592186696478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"a2e73bc8-691f-5620-b52d-5b2eacb05674\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{8}\" :db/id 17592186696471} :answer-field/id #uuid \"e83741ef-cdb1-5b76-aa16-1dbcd77031dd\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186696483}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"d5d5532c-d9d1-5837-8ecd-a43746e5a051\" :question/problem \"Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\\n$$\\n\\\\sin\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{12}\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{12}\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{6}\\\\right).\\n$$\\nUse $2\\\\sin x\\\\cos x=\\\\sin(2x)$, first with $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{12}$ and then with $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{6}$.\" :question/worked-solution \"Let $E$ denote the given expression. Use $\\\\sin x\\\\cos x=\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\sin(2x)$ first at $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{12}$ and then at $x=\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{6}$. Each application introduces a factor of $\\\\frac{1}{2}$.\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\nE&=\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\,\\\\sin\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{6}\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{6}\\\\right)\\\\\\\\&=\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\,\\\\sin\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{3}\\\\right)\\n\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\nThe terminal sine is $\\\\sin\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\pi}{3}\\\\right)=\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{2}$.\\nTherefore,\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\nE&=\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\,\\\\left(\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\\\right)\\\\\\\\&=\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{8}.\\n\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186696484 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"029d687d-6bdf-5d50-8a26-c12c66256da2\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3 \\\\sqrt{2}}{8}\" :db/id 17592186696459} {:answer/id #uuid \"712db24e-43d4-5a1d-b599-e01f890e7e79\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{2}\" :db/id 17592186696468} {:answer/id #uuid \"e0ffbda3-c70a-5f23-b5f9-354169308143\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{16}\" :db/id 17592186696480} {:answer/id #uuid \"e17c5967-20fa-530e-9463-59c2e621fc67\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3 \\\\sqrt{3}}{16}\" :db/id 17592186696481} {:answer/id #uuid \"f0701d0a-791a-5a5a-a979-907175f778ef\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{8}\" :db/id 17592186696485}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"f0701d0a-791a-5a5a-a979-907175f778ef\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{8}\" :db/id 17592186696485} :answer-field/id #uuid \"a02b09aa-0f6d-5f2b-bef1-f293b52b1e3a\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186696470}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"efb73604-909d-53a0-ae97-6e34be06688f\" :question/problem \"Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\\n$$\\n3\\\\,\\\\sin\\\\left(7.5^\\\\circ\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(7.5^\\\\circ\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(15^\\\\circ\\\\right).\\n$$\\nUse $2\\\\sin x\\\\cos x=\\\\sin(2x)$, first with $x=7.5^\\\\circ$ and then with $x=15^\\\\circ$.\" :question/worked-solution \"Let $E$ denote the given expression. Use $\\\\sin x\\\\cos x=\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\sin(2x)$ first at $x=7.5^\\\\circ$ and then at $x=15^\\\\circ$. Each application introduces a factor of $\\\\frac{1}{2}$.\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\nE&=\\\\frac{3}{2}\\\\,\\\\sin\\\\left(15^\\\\circ\\\\right)\\\\cos\\\\left(15^\\\\circ\\\\right)\\\\\\\\&=\\\\frac{3}{4}\\\\,\\\\sin\\\\left(30^\\\\circ\\\\right)\\n\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\nThe terminal sine is $\\\\sin\\\\left(30^\\\\circ\\\\right)=\\\\frac{1}{2}$.\\nTherefore,\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\nE&=\\\\frac{3}{4}\\\\,\\\\left(\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\right)\\\\\\\\&=\\\\frac{3}{8}.\\n\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"}] :knowledge-point/title \"Using the Double-Angle Formula Multiple Times\"}",
